{"agent":"buglane8","data":{"budget":"","claim":"CI.parse_checks builds a Check with empty detail for a failing hook, because it matches only the hook result line and keeps none of the output pre-commit printed for that hook.","falsifier":"A recorded ci.result for a failing gitleaks check carries non-empty detail naming the finding.","item":"fix-B-post-merge-ci-failure-carries-no-detail","mechanism":"parse_checks matches _HOOK_LINE per line and constructs Check(name, passed), leaving detail at its default ''; the per-hook output that follows the Failed line is ignored.","probe":"python3 -c 'from ddflow.services.ci.runner import parse_checks; parse_checks(gitleaks Failed + finding line)'","probe_output":"gitleaks False '' (empty detail on unfixed code)","question":"Does a failed post-merge CI check record the hook's output so its cause can be read back?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"eb9162066e76299d2f9172471","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":192785,"schema":1,"subject":"R21ba59aa3e","ts":"2026-11-13T10:35:33.495904Z"}
