{"agent":"buglane8","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new detail collector treats a `Skipped` hook line as ordinary output belonging to the previous failed hook. For a line such as `bandit.......Skipped`, the `if m and m[\"status\"] != \"Skipped\":` branch is false, so execution falls into `elif failed is not None:` and appends the skipped-hook line (and any following non-hook lines) to the failed hook’s `lines`. Given a report like:\n\n```text\ngitleaks.......Failed\nsecret in file.txt\nbandit.......Skipped\nbandit skipped for merge\n```\n\nthe `gitleaks` check’s `detail` will include `bandit.......Skipped` and `bandit skipped for merge`, not only the gitleaks output. If the skipped hook’s text is long, the 2000-character tail can push out the actual `secret in file.txt` line, which is exactly the kind of missing/misleading detail this change is supposed to prevent. A `Skipped` hook line should terminate the current failed hook’s detail, even though it should not be appended as a check.","digest":"cdcd42153d68d263","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:parse_checks","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:parse_checks"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":3466,"diff_sha":"7dbd956ca3d9a4727a67448030b1ee0f904dbe0518bdeec7b49d21e88e39c967","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-post-merge-ci-failure-carries-no-detail","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":0.7,"family":"alibaba","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"0c8d0abc3df67f6a","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-post-merge-ci-failure-carries-no-detail.critic.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261113T113824Z-2babe930.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_he