{"agent":"buglane8","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new detail collector treats a `Skipped` hook line as ordinary output belonging to the previous failed hook. For a line such as `bandit.......Skipped`, the `if m and m[\"status\"] != \"Skipped\":` branch is false, so execution falls into `elif failed is not None:` and appends the skipped-hook line (and any following non-hook lines) to the failed hook’s `lines`. Given a report like:\n\n```text\ngitleaks.......Failed\nsecret in file.txt\nbandit.......Skipped\nbandit skipped for merge\n```\n\nthe `gitleaks` check’s `detail` will include `bandit.......Skipped` and `bandit skipped for merge`, not only the gitleaks output. If the skipped hook’s text is long, the 2000-character tail can push out the actual `secret in file.txt` line, which is exactly the kind of missing/misleading detail this change is supposed to prevent. A `Skipped` hook line should terminate the current failed hook’s detail, even though it should not be appended as a check.","digest":"cdcd42153d68d263","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:parse_checks","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:parse_checks"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new `if m:` boundary test treats every `_HOOK_LINE` match as a hook result line, but the regex has no word boundary before the status word, so it also matches lines where `Skipped` is only a suffix of a larger token. For example, given a failed hook whose output contains the flush-left line `check.......NotSkipped` followed by the actual finding `finding: secret`, the second line matches with `status=\"Skipped\"`; parse_checks flushes the failed hook’s detail (empty if this is the first output line) and then discards the subsequent finding, leaving `detail=\"\"`. The previous code appended `Skipped`-status matches to the failed hook’s lines, so this is a regression introduced by making all regex matches boundaries.","digest":"0b73524d28b96521","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:parse_checks","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:parse_checks"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":1,"delta_from":"88d16c515bed26d46d472a09e58b8ad5b21e206e","delta_raised":["0b73524d28b96521"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":2969,"diff_sha":"0a6c0a0770acdf87690862795202cf9bf89b346c8f2c2ca3718d288613994a1a","diff_source":"delta review of 2 commits since 88d16c515b","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":0.9,"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"full_coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"247c04c79c1a6999","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-post-merge-ci-failure-carries-no-detail.critic.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261113T115430Z-78633c35.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"faecefce12ce5287ad4ce700fe1586e1825351b4","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py":"100644 0575d13ec1cbedad8e97cfbb9b3b282d35ca9899","tests/test_ci_main_check.py":"100644 ac693b741f44e27fc2ef16c83335b6704d404c5d"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba","google"],"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:parse_checks","ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:parse_checks"],"tree_sha":"faecefce12ce+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"eb657e62695967ee059cd04d1","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":193202,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-post-merge-ci-failure-carries-no-detail","ts":"2026-11-13T11:54:31.610214Z"}
